  "findings": [
    "Source sweatshirt is already one connected shell; no disconnected shoulder components exist.",
    "Neck opening is a closed 148-edge loop, .366 m wide, centered [.811817,0,1.223884]; two cuff loops44 each and hem72 make308 boundary edges.",
    "Separate folded hood is a closed doubled cloth shell, not welded to sweatshirt.",
    "author_garments.py and author_hood.py expect obsolete rider:hoodie object and ring counts; neither can run directly on current source. No current anatomical sweatshirt creation script found in assets/blender.",
    "Current failed trial works on exported UV-split geometry and appends six collar rings rather than rebuilding wide source neck/shoulder transition; this preserves original broad uneven opening."
  ],
  "recommendedEdit": [
    "Work on a copy of exact source anatomical sweatshirt, not source regeneration. Identify148-edge neck boundary topologically and fair its surrounding two-to-four face rings as one surface.",
    "Build neck boundary fit against actual saved head/neck transformed into source coordinates. Narrow and reposition whole transition with smooth falloff through shoulder/chest rather than filling a broad gap with radial fans.",
    "Give neckline a narrow rolled edge and intentional thickness; connect hood mouth to rear neckline or seat it physically without visible floating overlap.",
    "Preserve existing distal sleeve/torso vertex weights; interpolate boundary weights from chest/neck and validate every clip. Bake continuous UV/material region instead of recycled per-triangle atlas patches.",
    "For active exported mesh, map source garment by UV correspondence or exact triangle mapping; position-only matching becomes unreliable after earlier cloth smoothing. Keep six clips and saved head attachment unchanged."
  ],
  "limitations": "Read-only topology diagnosis; source intersections and aesthetic acceptance not proven by these metrics. Parent must judge motion."
